Linear Search 🔎:
Start from the first element and compare every element with the target.

Algorithm:
1. Start from index 0
2. Compare current element with target
3. If equal → return index
4. Otherwise move to next element
5. If we reach the end → element doesn't exist

Pseudocode:
LinearSearch(A, n, target)
for i = 0 to n-1
    if A[i] == target
        return i

return -1

Now, the actual code:

#include <stdio.h>
int linearSearch(int arr[], int n, int target)
{
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
    {
        if (arr[i] == target)
        {
            return i;
        }
    }
    return -1;
}

int main()
{
    int arr[] = {10, 25, 7, 42, 18};
    int n = 5;
    int target = 42;

    int result = linearSearch(arr, n, target);

    if (result != -1)
        printf("Element found at index %d\n", result);
    else
        printf("Element not found\n");

    return 0;
}


| Case    | Complexity |
| ------- | ---------- |
| Best    |   O(1)   |
| Average |   O(n)   |
| Worst   |   O(n)   |
| Space   |   O(1)   |


Binary Search

it repeatedly cuts the search area in half.

Algo:
BinarySearch(A, n, key)

1. Start
2. Set low = 0
3. Set high = n - 1
4. While low <= high:
      mid = (low + high) / 2

      If A[mid] == key:
          Return mid

      Else if A[mid] < key:
          low = mid + 1

      Else:
          high = mid - 1

5. Return -1
6. Stop


Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int binarySearch(int A[], int n, int key)
{
    int low = 0;
    int high = n - 1;

    while (low <= high)
    {
        int mid = (low + high) / 2;

        if (A[mid] == key)
            return mid;

        else if (A[mid] < key)
            low = mid + 1;

        else
            high = mid - 1;
    }

    return -1;
}

int main()
{
    int A[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70};
    int n = 7;
    int key = 60;

    int result = binarySearch(A, n, key);

    if (result != -1)
        printf("Element found at index %d", result);
    else
        printf("Element not found");

    return 0;
}

Complexity:
Best: O(1)
Average: O(log n)
Worst: O(log n)
Space: O(1)


Linear search:

Works on sorted or unsorted arrays.
Checks elements one by one.
Start from index 0.

Loop condition is usually:

i < n

Compare:

A[i] == key
If found → return/print the index.
If the loop finishes → element is not found.

Commonly return:

-1

to indicate "not found".

⚠️ Watch out for

Array index vs position

For:
A = [10, 20, 30]
Index:     0   1   2
Position:  1   2   3
